h2>=0D=0A                            <p class=3D"corner-intro">A collection=
 of web design and development news and thoughts from CodePen's own Chris C=
oyier.</p>=0D=0A                          </mj-raw>=0D=0A                  =
        <h3>Processing</h3>=0D=0A<p>The other week when I was <a href=3D"ht=
tps://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/A9k-S0iN9zJxSilGIW5wZQ~~/AABEfhA~/nR-ogLmeV=
6QYJHYYPr_pJz8oEb7VxKnZLLavIdlZSyD2ub2fctvdfsc4ENY-E3zT4s4LH0tOSPrkL4fDm5k0=
rGNZDg4noHG_06UL45KWBHGWo2NRHdXZ4z-61mKb4xeHohVaqYxA_SYWTmmTkktatu-YyHFXd3r=
08e6pGvAY6kU~">talking about Web Components in the Corner</a>, I mentioned =
<a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/9WTUuz5KaAg-1fS0WNTzkg~~/AABEf=
hA~/uSEMdC5D72QmM_2-t_lJcqlKmiXuUvXxPsLg0-gSz6HDWEx-d9A6eTyV72UCbYilv4ncagg=
6-I05AZesYHBjhPpldYYRGsQ2ThdDUipjF3h9uE8OKJIhy0oeOmYq6EKRkW7bBRPAe6aXIVQ_y9=
ym6g~~">zero-md</a>, a nice little Web Component for doing exactly that. I =
had to bite my tongue a little bit though, as <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpo=
stmail2.com/f/a/1WgIgAEQvTvNeoRFY5fzNg~~/AABEfhA~/8ATGvShx-rAypf7hJIQmzhQmz=
zOGZSFNx1Wzp2X6_4V2KSCVrswXslH1ak6mH-XfLP_nzOrCHEpabVdH83D63X9HMRqHONzklH2H=
HGoaEL64QxeGXD5ru4lH3YpL72LZ">the 2.0 public beta</a> hadn=E2=80=99t quite =
made it out of the door yet.</p>=0D=0A<p>See, <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpo=
stmail2.com/f/a/F2-5Ry29OPrEv8z2P-kj2Q~~/AABEfhA~/gml3xvwkSVDkyT3istQr3lNfo=
5ACjm18hUosaVfSeJQnnfPa-l9xPGbERD-3MykVtd1U-KP7sESlcl-Z4cnJNup3OomSXfwFHJZb=
09sNwefu3UvEKGtap4aepxg2SRmE">the new compiler</a>, among its many powers, =
has a cool trick up its sleeve we call <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2=
.com/f/a/i_hrscaHRePLsOHJX4DwMA~~/AABEfhA~/1nQlSvh-UgcNzdV0si5T6C6kd_D8e2z=
0DzUkMUBXhq6AkTeYvZfThyNjgCWwK4z7PoFX6-j0rVZT6bwhsCOu-Mk0DiUOtqav3kOdoUpslB=
C911yL8ihMxm7OF5RksZ2YBkAoj6R3_n3edt7Mt1bZUNWvb8-3zYJoTwTK3Y8xCMU~">Inline =
Block Processing</a>. When you=E2=80=99re in any HTML-ish language, you=E2=
=80=99ve got the lang attribute you can put on elements. Our compiler sees =
those, and if the language matches a <em>file extension</em> that we curren=
tly support via Blocks, we=E2=80=99ll process the <em>content</em> of that =
element with that block.</p>=0D=0A<p>Meaning you could write HTML like this=
:</p>=0D=0A=0D=0A<pre><code class=3D"html">&lt;p&gt;Blah blah just hanging =
out.&lt;/p&gt;=0D=0A&lt;div lang=3D&quot;md&quot;&gt;=0D=0A- I'm a list =0D=
=0A- in Markdown format =0D=0A- cool, right=3F=0D=0A&lt;/div&gt;=0D=0A&lt;s=
tyle lang=3D&quot;scss&quot;&gt;=0D=0A$listColor: red;=0D=0Aul {=0D=0A  col=
or: $listColor;=0D=0A  }=0D=0A&lt;/style&gt;=0D=0A</code></pre>=0D=0A=0D=0A=
<p>And that will=E2=80=A6 work. As you might be able to guess, it does. In =
the final processed code, the <code>lang</code> attributes are removed and =
the guts of those elements are replaced with the processed code produced by=
 the relevant Block.</p>=0D=0A<p>It=E2=80=99s just a neat little ability! I=
n the case of Markdown, it=E2=80=99s especially useful, and means you don=
=E2=80=99t need to reach for a client-side tool like zero-md, because the p=
rocessing happens server-side, which is good for performance.</p>=0D=0A<hr =
/>=0D=0A<p>Avoiding tools, or downshifting tools from client to server, alw=
ays has a nice feeling to me.</p>=0D=0A<p>Blake Watson has a presentation-a=
rticle <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/q7TyDit00n79h4M6Mgj87g~=
~/AABEfhA~/o13naYoUmtKgGgPD38SGl9D9IEd1IbFdZ-bx5BGAPzMrFPzRBOjp2jy1m9GbxnFf=
7TrZsD7l7DKAGZ0TIqHPc8aEjqPt0LJIj_preUMaNzi7VXou2zGzwR2WscCAK43MK7cNBVf6GG1=
04L9-NAdHrI6SdCiY5EM0wo4fNAi5mwFCnfYhvP4JZxaiaAiOvqVV">No build tool=3F No =
problem!</a> that has nice basic explanations of the tradeoffs. Like, is Ty=
peScript useful=3F Of course it can be. Does it mean complicating your work=
flow=3F Yep. Now you=E2=80=99ve got a whole chain of dependencies to potent=
ially worry about, and the potential for things to break, especially over t=
ime. It doesn=E2=80=99t mean don=E2=80=99t use it, but it=E2=80=99s worth t=
hinking about, especially when there are interesting alternatives. JSDoc is=
 the obvious one, but Blake points out you can just put <code>// @ts-check<=
/code> on the top of files and VS Code will TypeScript check a regular Java=
Script file, which is pretty interesting. I=E2=80=99d hope CodePen makes ch=
oosing tools a bit more palatable as well, since there is no setup cost and=
 it won=E2=80=99t break over time, as the tool choices are locked in foreve=
r until you change them.</p>=0D=0A<hr />=0D=0A<p>While considering build to=
ols a bit, it feels like an interesting time to consider if AI could be (re=
place=3F) a build tool. Here=E2=80=99s an example. RIGHT THIS SECOND can yo=
u remember how to write a loop in Sass code=3F Or is it something you gotta=
 look up=3F If you=E2=80=99re like me, I always try to find a reference to =
